sequenceDiagram
    participant R1 as Request 1
    participant Conn as Pooled Connection
    participant R2 as Request 2

    Note over R1,R2: Scenario 1 - session lock leaks across requests
    R1->>Conn: pg_advisory_lock(55001)
    Conn-->>R1: acquired
    Note right of R1: forgets to unlock
    R1->>Conn: done - connection returned to pool
    R2->>Conn: pg_try_advisory_lock(55001)
    Conn-->>R2: true - WRONG, inherited from Request 1
    Note over R1,R2: Request 2 believes it is alone. It only reused Request 1's session.

    Note over R1,R2: Scenario 2 - transaction lock cannot leak
    R1->>Conn: pg_advisory_xact_lock(55002)
    Conn-->>R1: acquired
    R1->>Conn: COMMIT
    Note right of Conn: released automatically - no unlock call to forget
    R2->>Conn: pg_try_advisory_lock(55002)
    Conn-->>R2: true - correctly free
